# remote-cluster-agent: Project Rule

This project uses the `remote-cluster-agent` skill for development on a remote GPU cluster. Claude Code auto-loads this file when sessions start in this project — these rules apply to **all** sessions here.

## 1. Sync before remote exec (both directions)

Mutagen syncs in near-real-time but is **not synchronous**. Two race conditions to avoid:

- **Local edit → remote exec**: file change may not have reached the cluster yet → `rca exec` runs **stale code**.
- **Remote exec → local read**: output file may not have synced back yet → `Read("outputs/...")` returns **stale content**.

**Fix**: flush before crossing the boundary.

```bash
# Before any rca exec that runs code you just edited:
mutagen sync flush {{MUTAGEN_SESSION}}
rca exec -n {{NODE}} "..."

# After rca exec writes to outputs/, before reading locally:
mutagen sync flush {{MUTAGEN_SESSION}}
# now Read("outputs/...") is safe
```

`mutagen sync flush` blocks until the session is fully propagated. Cost: ~50-100ms when nothing pending, ~200-500ms after a small edit.

**Exempt** (no flush needed) — pure queries that don't touch files you just changed:
`nvidia-smi`, `ps`, `df`, `uptime`, `tmux ls`, `conda env list`, `rca nodes`.

## 2. Local edit / remote execute — never run user code locally

| Operation | Where |
|-----------|-------|
| `Read` / `Edit` / `Write` / `Glob` / `Grep` | **Local** (mutagen mirrors to remote) |
| `python ...`, `pytest`, `pip install`, training, scripts | **Remote** (`rca exec -n {{NODE}}`) |
| Inspect synced output files | **Local** `Read("outputs/...")` (faster than SSH cat) |
| `nvidia-smi`, `ps`, status checks | **Remote** (`rca exec` or `rca batch`) |

The local machine does **not** have this project's runtime deps. Never run `python` / `pytest` / `pip` locally in this project.

## 3. Python on remote always uses conda env `{{CONDA_ENV}}`

Every `rca exec` Python invocation must activate `{{CONDA_ENV}}`. Recommended forms:

```bash
# For long jobs / tests with live output (use -s to stream):
rca exec -s -n {{NODE}} --stdin <<'EOF'
source {{CONDA_SH}}
conda activate {{CONDA_ENV}}
cd {{REMOTE_DIR}}
python <your-command>
EOF

# One-liner for short commands (no streaming):
rca exec -n {{NODE}} -d {{REMOTE_DIR}} "conda run -n {{CONDA_ENV}} python <your-command>"
```

Without activation: `python` on remote uses the system interpreter and **will not find this project's deps** (ModuleNotFoundError).

## Project info (recorded at init)

- Node: `{{NODE}}`
- Remote project dir: `{{REMOTE_DIR}}`
- Mutagen sync session: `{{MUTAGEN_SESSION}}`
- Conda env (on remote): `{{CONDA_ENV}}`
- Conda init script (on remote): `{{CONDA_SH}}`

